-- allium: 3
-- explanation.allium
--
-- Muṣarrif: Grammatical Explanation Engine
--
-- Scope: Turning a conjugated verb form or a derived nominal (masdar, active or
--        passive participle) into a structured explanation the learner can read,
--        and hiding parts of it once told which layers to hide.
-- Includes: explanation structure, sentence kinds, the grammatical layers an
--           explanation draws on and the root-interaction phenomena they can
--           name, layer-based hiding, the reduced form-only summary used by
--           verb-form browsing
-- Excludes:
--   - The phonological rule engine that decides WHICH interaction (if any)
--     applies for a given root type, form, tense and pronoun, and how it is
--     realised in the Arabic script — an extension of the conjugation-algorithm
--     exclusion in conjugate.allium
--   - Locale string content and translation mechanics
--   - Rendering: colour coding, morpheme markers, modal/panel placement
--     (see conjugate.allium and exercise.allium surfaces)
--   - Mastery computation itself (spaced-repetition intervals, thresholds) —
--     see exercise.allium; this spec only covers hiding, given a set of layers

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- One sentence of an explanation, tagged with the visual/conceptual category it
-- belongs to.
value ExplanationSentence {
    text: String
    kind: ExplanationKind
}

-- An explanation is computed on demand from a verb and a grammatical context — a
-- (tense, pronoun) pair for a conjugated verb form, or one of masdar, active
-- participle, passive participle for a derived nominal. Its sentences are grouped
-- into up to four paragraphs, in order: form and root, nominal pattern, tense and
-- voice, pronoun agreement. A paragraph left with no sentences is omitted, so an
-- explanation may carry fewer than four paragraphs, or in the extreme, none.
--
-- Verb-form browsing (see conjugate.allium's VerbBrowse surface) shows a reduced
-- explanation instead of the full one: only the form-and-root paragraph, always
-- generated for the citation form (3ms active past) regardless of which
-- conjugation the learner is currently viewing, and rendered as plain joined text
-- rather than kind-coloured sentences.
value Explanation {
    paragraphs: List<List<ExplanationSentence>>
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The visual/conceptual category a sentence belongs to. Consecutive sentences of
-- the same kind are grouped under one colour marker where a morpheme breakdown is
-- shown alongside the explanation.
--   radical:   root-phonology sentences — root type, and how form or tense
--              interacts with the root's weak or doubled letters
--   measure:   binyan/pattern sentences — form, vowel pattern, nominal pattern,
--              passive voice, imperative stem support
--   agreement: pronoun agreement and most tense sentences
--   particle:  the future-tense sentence (marked by a separate particle)
--   elided:    a dropped prefix, dropped suffix, or elided final radical
enum ExplanationKind { radical | measure | agreement | particle | elided }

-- The independently hideable pieces of context an explanation draws on. rootType
-- and form apply to both verb and nominal explanations; tense and pronoun apply to
-- verb explanations only; nominal applies to nominal explanations only.
enum ExplanationLayer { rootType | form | tense | pronoun | nominal }

-- The way Form VIII's infixed ت assimilates to the root's first radical. Applies
-- only to Form VIII, and only when that radical calls for it.
--   assimilationComplete: the infix becomes identical to the first radical
--   assimilationVoicing:  the infix becomes د (voicing assimilation)
--   assimilationEmphasis: the infix becomes ط (emphatic assimilation)
enum FormRootInteraction { assimilationComplete | assimilationVoicing | assimilationEmphasis }

-- How a verb's weak or doubled root radical interacts with the tense being
-- conjugated. Which one (if any) applies for a given root type, form, tense and
-- pronoun is excluded (see Excludes); this only names the phenomena.
--
-- Hollow roots (weak middle radical):
--   middleLengthensAa: the middle radical lengthens to a long ا in the past
--   middleLengthensUu: lengthens to a long و in the active present/future (waw roots)
--   middleLengthensIi: lengthens to a long ي in the active present/future (yaa roots)
--   middleShortens:    shortens in the jussive and imperative
--   middlePassiveAa:   lengthens to a long ا in the passive present
--   middlePassiveIi:   lengthens to a long ي in the passive past
--
-- Defective roots (weak final radical):
--   finalIsolated:    the final radical stands alone in the 3ms past
--   finalElides:      the final radical elides before a vowel-initial suffix (3fs, 3fd)
--   finalResurfaces:  the final radical resurfaces before a consonant-initial suffix
--   finalLengthensUu: lengthens to a long و in the active present/future (waw roots)
--   finalLengthensIi: lengthens to a long ي in the active present/future (yaa roots)
--   finalDrops:       drops in the jussive and imperative
--
-- Assimilated roots (weak initial radical, Form I only):
--   initialDrops: the initial و drops in the active present and future
--
-- Doubled and hamzated-doubled roots (identical final radicals):
--   geminateContracts: the two identical radicals contract into one doubled consonant
--   geminateJussive:   the radicals stay uncontracted in the jussive and imperative
--
-- Hamzated roots:
--   hamzaSeat: the hamza's seat letter (أ / إ / ؤ / ئ / ء) is chosen for the
--              surrounding vowels
enum TenseRootInteraction {
    finalDrops | finalElides | finalIsolated
        | finalLengthensIi | finalLengthensUu | finalResurfaces
        | geminateContracts | geminateJussive
        | hamzaSeat | initialDrops
        | middleLengthensAa | middleLengthensIi | middleLengthensUu
        | middlePassiveAa | middlePassiveIi | middleShortens
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Layer Visibility
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An explanation can be narrowed to a subset of visible ExplanationLayers —
-- consumed by exercise.allium to fade out material the learner has already
-- mastered (see its own scope for how "mastered" is decided; this spec only
-- covers the hiding itself, given a set of hidden layers).
--
-- Hiding a layer removes the sentences it alone is responsible for:
--   rootType hidden  -> the root-type sentence is removed
--   form hidden      -> the vowel-pattern and form sentences are removed
--   tense hidden     -> the tense and voice sentences are removed
--   pronoun hidden   -> the pronoun agreement, dropped-prefix and dropped-suffix
--                       sentences are removed
--   nominal hidden   -> the nominal-pattern sentence is removed
--
-- Two sentences describe how the root's weak or doubled letters interact with
-- form or tense, and so depend on rootType as well as their own layer: the
-- form-root sentence is removed only once BOTH form and rootType are hidden, and
-- the tense-root sentence only once BOTH tense and rootType are hidden. While
-- either layer in the pair stays visible, the sentence stays.
--
-- A paragraph left with no visible sentences is omitted.
